.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH http 1  "http " 
.SH NAME
http \- HTTP/1.1 exchanges: send request(s), dissect the responses
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBhttp\fR [\fB\-i\fR|\fB\-\-iface\fR] [\fB\-\-format\fR] [\fB\-v \fR]... [\fB\-\-no\-autofill\fR] [\fB\-\-strict\fR] [\fB\-H\fR|\fB\-\-header\fR] [\fB\-\-data\fR] [\fB\-\-recipe\fR] [\fB\-\-timeout\fR] [\fB\-\-retries\fR] [\fB\-\-max\-bytes\fR] [\fB\-\-source\-port\fR] [\fB\-\-tls\-insecure\fR] [\fB\-\-tls\-ca\fR] [\fB\-\-http\-version\fR] [\fB\-\-hpack\fR] [\fB\-L\fR|\fB\-\-follow\fR] [\fB\-\-max\-redirs\fR] [\fB\-b\fR|\fB\-\-cookie\fR] [\fB\-c\fR|\fB\-\-cookie\-jar\fR] [\fB\-\-fail\fR] [\fB\-u\fR|\fB\-\-user\fR] [\fB\-\-bearer\fR] [\fB\-\-digest\fR] [\fB\-\-compressed\fR] [\fB\-o\fR|\fB\-\-output\fR] [\fB\-O\fR|\fB\-\-remote\-name\fR] [\fB\-T\fR|\fB\-\-upload\-file\fR] [\fB\-I\fR|\fB\-\-head\fR] [\fB\-\-include\fR] [\fB\-r\fR|\fB\-\-range\fR] [\fB\-\-resolve\fR] [\fB\-\-retry\fR] [\fB\-x\fR|\fB\-\-proxy\fR] [\fB\-U\fR|\fB\-\-proxy\-user\fR] [\fB\-\-timing\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fIURL_OR_METHOD\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
HTTP/1.1 exchanges: send request(s), dissect the responses
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-i\fR, \fB\-\-iface\fR \fI<IFACE>\fR
Interface for send/recv
.TP
\fB\-\-format\fR \fI<FORMAT>\fR
Output format: raw|hex|text|json|jsonl
.TP
\fB\-v\fR
Verbosity (repeatable: \-v info, \-vv debug, \-vvv trace)
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-autofill\fR
Disable every autofill/derivation (unspecified numeric fields → 0)
.TP
\fB\-\-strict\fR
Validate the crafted packet after encode (violations → exit 2)
.TP
\fB\-H\fR, \fB\-\-header\fR \fI<NAME:VALUE>\fR
Request header, repeatable (NAME:VALUE)
.TP
\fB\-\-data\fR \fI<TEXT|@FILE|hex:…>\fR
Request body: literal text, @FILE or hex:BYTES
.TP
\fB\-\-recipe\fR \fI<FILE>\fR
Replay a recipe file (method/url/headers/body in JSON)
.TP
\fB\-\-timeout\fR \fI<TIMEOUT>\fR
Per\-attempt exchange timeout (default 10s)
.TP
\fB\-\-retries\fR \fI<RETRIES>\fR
Extra attempts beyond the first on timeout/truncation (default 0)
.TP
\fB\-\-max\-bytes\fR \fI<MAX_BYTES>\fR
Response byte budget, head included (default 64 MiB)
.TP
\fB\-\-source\-port\fR \fI<SOURCE_PORT>\fR
Bind this local source port (determinism on multihomed hosts)
.TP
\fB\-\-tls\-insecure\fR
Accept any server certificate for https:// (dangerous; no name/chain/validity check)
.TP
\fB\-\-tls\-ca\fR \fI<FILE>\fR
Extra CA bundle, PEM or DER (complements the system roots)
.TP
\fB\-\-http\-version\fR \fI<1.1|2>\fR
HTTP version: `1.1` (default) or `2` — for https, h2 rides ALPN (`h2` then `http/1.1`; a server that declines h2 falls back to HTTP/1.1 with a note); for http, h2 is cleartext **prior knowledge** (RFC 9113 §3.4: the preface goes straight over the TCP stream, no `Upgrade:` dance). Recipe wins over the flag
.TP
\fB\-\-hpack\fR \fI<indexed|literal>\fR
Send\-side HPACK policy for h2 (tranche 16a): `indexed` (default: dynamic table + Huffman\-when\-strictly\-shorter) or `literal` (the pre\-16 wire bytes: indexed statics, no dynamic\-table state, never Huffman — the replay\-parity knob). Recipe wins over the flag; inert on 1.1 runs
.TP
\fB\-L\fR, \fB\-\-follow\fR
Follow 3xx redirects (tranche 19a): Location resolution per RFC 3986, method rules per RFC 9110 §15.4 + curl (303 ⇒ GET, 301/302 rewrite POST ⇒ GET, 307/308 preserve; Authorization drops on a cross\-origin hop). Same\-origin hops ride the open connection; `\-\-format json` adds `url` + `redirects` keys
.TP
\fB\-\-max\-redirs\fR \fI<N>\fR
Redirect hop budget under \-\-follow (default 50, curl\*(Aqs)
.TP
\fB\-b\fR, \fB\-\-cookie\fR \fI<FILE|VALUE>\fR
Cookie input (tranche 19a): a Netscape\-format jar file (curl \-b), or — when the string is not a readable file — a literal `Cookie:` header value. With a jar, the jar owns the Cookie header on every request (an explicit \-H Cookie does not survive it); Set\-Cookie responses update it
.TP
\fB\-c\fR, \fB\-\-cookie\-jar\fR \fI<FILE>\fR
Write the (updated) cookie jar here on exit, Netscape format (curl \-c); implies a jar even without \-b (collect\-only)
.TP
\fB\-\-fail\fR
Exit 1 on 4xx/5xx statuses (completed exchanges stay data)
.TP
\fB\-u\fR, \fB\-\-user\fR \fI<USER[:PASS]>\fR
Basic\-auth credentials (tranche 19a): `Authorization: Basic` on every request (curl \-u). USER alone = empty password
.TP
\fB\-\-bearer\fR \fI<TOKEN>\fR
`Authorization: Bearer TOKEN` on every request (exclusive with \-\-user)
.TP
\fB\-\-digest\fR
With \-\-user: answer a `401` carrying a Digest challenge via the RFC 7616 dance (no preemptive header; MD5, MD5\-sess, SHA\-256, SHA\-256\-sess, qop=auth and the legacy no\-qop shape; a Basic\-only 401 stays data)
.TP
\fB\-\-compressed\fR
Request compressed content (tranche 19a): advertise the four codecs wrex decodes — `deflate, gzip, br, zstd` (curl\*(Aqs list, byte\-exact) — and decode `Content\-Encoding` responses (stacked codings right\-to\-left; the raw deflate fallback; multi\-member gzip). Decoded bytes count against \-\-max\-bytes exactly like wire bytes (the bomb cap)
.TP
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-output\fR \fI<FILE>\fR
Write the response BODY to FILE, one \-o per URL in order (curl \-o); responses past the last \-o go to stdout. Exclusive with \-O
.TP
\fB\-O\fR, \fB\-\-remote\-name\fR
Write the body to the URL\*(Aqs remote basename in the CWD (curl \-O). Exclusive with \-o
.TP
\fB\-T\fR, \fB\-\-upload\-file\fR \fI<FILE>\fR
Upload FILE: PUT with the file bytes as the body (curl \-T; exclusive with \-\-data)
.TP
\fB\-I\fR, \fB\-\-head\fR
HEAD request (curl \-I; exclusive with an explicit METHOD)
.TP
\fB\-\-include\fR
Include the response head in raw output (curl \-i; \-\-format text always carries it)
.TP
\fB\-r\fR, \fB\-\-range\fR \fI<SPEC>\fR
Range request sugar: `Range: bytes=<SPEC>` (curl \-r; SPEC is `N\-M`, `N\-` or `\-N`)
.TP
\fB\-\-resolve\fR \fI<HOST[:PORT]:ADDR>\fR
Pin a hostname to an address, bypassing resolution (curl \-\-resolve `HOST[:PORT]:ADDR`, repeatable; applies to redirect hops too)
.TP
\fB\-\-retry\fR \fI<N>\fR
Retry on transient response statuses: N extra attempts when a completed response is 5xx (per request, fresh exchange — no delay; curl\*(Aqs backoff is deliberately not implemented, the lab\-tool deviation)
.TP
\fB\-x\fR, \fB\-\-proxy\fR \fI<[SCHEME://]HOST:PORT>\fR
Route through a proxy (tranche 19b, curl \-x): `[http://]` an HTTP proxy (absolute\-form request\-targets for http://, CONNECT tunnels for https://), `socks5://` (local resolution) or `socks5h://` (the proxy resolves). Applies to redirect hops
.TP
\fB\-U\fR, \fB\-\-proxy\-user\fR \fI<USER[:PASS]>\fR
Proxy credentials (curl \-U `USER[:PASS]`): Basic for CONNECT, RFC 1929 for SOCKS5
.TP
\fB\-\-timing\fR
Add a `timing` object to each `\-\-format json` response: time_connect_ms / time_appconnect_ms (TLS, https only) / time_starttransfer_ms / time_total_ms — the curl \-w fields, json\-shaped. Per original request (a redirect chain\*(Aqs timings span its hops)
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
[\fIURL_OR_METHOD\fR]
Positional grammar: [METHOD] URL [URL...] (a URL\-looking first token ⇒ GET + a URL list; more URLs ride one keep\-alive connection, tranche 9a). Declared as one vec so clap cannot mis\-assign a URL to the method slot
.SH EXTRA
HTTP GRAMMAR:
  wrex http [METHOD] URL [URL...] [\-H NAME:VALUE]... [\-\-data TEXT|@FILE|hex:…]
           [\-\-timeout DUR] [\-\-retries N] [\-\-max\-bytes N]
           [\-\-source\-port N] [\-\-fail] [\-\-recipe FILE]
           [\-\-tls\-insecure] [\-\-tls\-ca FILE]
           [\-\-format text|json|raw]

  One URL (or a lone \-\-recipe object) is the tranche\-4 close mode:
  one exchange per connection (Connection: close). Multiple URLs
  (or a recipe array / {"requests": [...]} file) ride ONE
  keep\-alive connection in order — every request but the last
  carries Connection: keep\-alive; a response that says close (or
  HTTP/1.0, or read\-to\-close framing) ends the queue there.

  Requests are fully materialized first, so the same arguments (or
  the same \-\-recipe FILE) replay byte\-identical wire bytes. Host,
  User\-Agent, Accept and Content\-Length derive automatically with
  explicit\-wins semantics (user headers come first, in order);
  \-H/\-\-data apply to every URL of a multi\-URL run.

  Bodies: content\-length and chunked (trailers merge into headers),
  read\-to\-close when neither is declared; recipe body_framing
  "chunked" switches the REQUEST to fixed\-size chunks (chunk_size,
  default 4096 — deterministic). 1xx skipped; HEAD/204/304 carry no
  body. https:// rides TLS (the rustls engine behind the wrex\-tls
  driver adapter): SNI from the URL host, system roots plus optional
  \-\-tls\-ca FILE additions (PEM or DER); \-\-tls\-insecure accepts ANY
  certificate (dangerous: no name/chain/validity check — for lab
  targets).

  Any completed run is exit 0 whatever the statuses say; \-\-fail
  turns any 4xx/5xx into exit 1 (after printing); connect/timeout/
  protocol failures are exit 1; grammar and recipe errors are exit 2.

RECIPE (\-\-recipe FILE, JSON):
  {"method": "POST", "url": "https://host/api",
   "headers": [["X\-A", "1"]], "body_hex": "deadbeef",
   "body_framing": "chunked", "chunk_size": 4096,
   "timeout_ms": 1500, "retries": 1, "max_bytes": 67108864,
   "tls_insecure": false, "tls_ca": "ca.pem"}
  A queue is a top\-level array of such objects or
  {"requests": [obj, obj, …]} (one keep\-alive connection, in
  order). Ordered header pairs keep wire bytes deterministic;
  body_hex and body_text are mutually exclusive. tls_insecure/tls_ca
  are additive (defaults: off/absent) and honored for https urls.

EXAMPLES:
  wrex http http://example.com/
  wrex http POST http://example.com/api \-H X\-Thing:42 \-\-data \*(Aq{"a":1}\*(Aq
  wrex http http://example.com/a http://example.com/b   # one connection
  wrex http \-\-recipe req.json \-\-format json
  wrex http https://example.com/ \-\-tls\-insecure
  wrex http https://example.com/ \-\-tls\-ca myca.pem
  wrex http GET http://example.com/ \-\-data @body.bin \-\-source\-port 42424
